  "presentation_summary": [
    "42-year-old man presented to his general practitioner with sore throat and fever.",
    "The next day he had pharyngitis, enlarged submandibular lymph nodes, white coating of tonsils, and leukocytes in urine; amoxicillin-clavulanate was started.",
    "Two days later he developed generalized maculopapular rash and was admitted with fever 38.5 C and loose feces.",
    "Blood tests on admission showed WBC 7.0 x10^9/L with 15% lymphocytes, hemoglobin 13.6 g/dL, CRP 168 mg/L, AST 500 U/L, ALT 400 U/L, GGT 200 U/L, and bilirubin 36 umol/L.",
    "On the second hospital day he collapsed with massive hematochezia, shock, and hemoglobin 6.6 g/dL; colonoscopy and surgery found a single bleeding ulcer in the ascending colon.",
    "Infectious evaluation of the colon was negative for CMV, HSV, VZV, EBV, HHV6, adenovirus, enterovirus, Salmonella, Shigella, Campylobacter, Yersinia, Giardia, Entamoeba, Cryptosporidium, and acid-fast bacilli.",
    "HIV testing showed a negative HIV antibody test five months earlier, high HIV RNA 3.6 x10^7 copies/mL, and a subsequently evolving immunoblot consistent with primary HIV infection."
  ],
